   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<div lang=\"SV\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\n\n<div>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Hi<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">I am wondering about how randomForest is predicting\nthe weather (weather.csv).<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Is it looking at one row (day) before or many rows (days)\nbefore when it makes the predictions? Since it is a prediction for the rain\ntomorrow it can’t be on the same row.<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Or is the “RainTomorrow” column adjusted one\nstep down? <u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">(And is the “RainTomorrow” data used as\nsomething to build the prediction for the next row on?)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">What is the difference between classification and\nregression? Is it possible to see the difference in this example?<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Kind regards<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Rolf<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\n\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n\n"
    ]
